      "borderWidth": 4,
      "fontColor": "#0f172a",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "note": "The verifier, and the counterparty. On the person register the verifier is singular and is the beneficiary. Here it is plural — which only works if it is a GROUP. An individual is the wrong level, and a crowd captures.",
      "type": "lg_place",
      "icon": "rcn_gathering",
      "ovr": {
        "icon": "rcn_gathering"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kindness",
      "label": "KINDNESS",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 1460,
      "w": 78,
      "h": 78,
      "shape": "rect",
      "color": "#ccfbf1",
      "borderColor": "#0f766e",
      "borderWidth": 3,
      "fontColor": "#0f766e",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "note": "Love / Kindness -> Group is a positive link in your own frame, and it is upstream of everything else here. It is also the link nobody funds, which is why groups are so often assumed rather than made.",
      "type": "lg_cond",
      "icon": "rcn_trust",
      "ovr": {
        "icon": "rcn_trust"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "belonging",
      "label": "BELONGING",
      "x": 1360,
      "y": 1460,
      "w": 78,
      "h": 78,
      "shape": "rect",
      "color": "#ccfbf1",
      "borderColor": "#0f766e",
      "borderWidth": 3,
      "fontColor": "#0f766e",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "note": "The hub of the group level. It feeds Support, Learning, Sharing and Safety, and it is what carries the group level up into the large-system level — Fairness into Good, Diversity into Truth, Cooperation into Utility.",
      "type": "lg_cond",
      "icon": "rcn_support_network",
      "ovr": {
        "icon": "rcn_support_network"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "safety",
      "label": "SAFETY",
      "x": 1580,
      "y": 1460,
      "w": 78,
      "h": 78,
      "shape": "rect",
      "color": "#ccfbf1",
      "borderColor": "#0f766e",
      "borderWidth": 3,
      "fontColor": "#0f766e",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "note": "Belonging -> Safety, and Safety suppresses Fear. This is the load-bearing pair: without safety there is no honest verification, only the answer people think is expected of them.",
      "type": "lg_cond",
      "icon": "rcn_shelter",
      "ovr": {
        "icon": "rcn_shelter"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "size",
      "label": "GROUP SIZE",
      "x": 1140,
      "y": 1620,
      "w": 78,
      "h": 78,
      "shape": "rect",
      "color": "#ccfbf1",
      "borderColor": "#0f766e",
      "borderWidth": 3,
      "fontColor": "#0f766e",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "note": "Group Size -> Belonging is NEGATIVE in your frame. So bounded size is a design requirement, not a preference — it is the single parameter that decides whether a verifying body is a group or a crowd. It also sets how big a polygon can be.",
      "type": "lg_cond",
      "icon": "rcn_boundary",
      "ovr": {
        "icon": "rcn_boundary"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "talk",
      "label": "ONGOING DELIBERATIVE CONVERSATION",
      "x": 1360,
      "y": 1620,
      "w": 78,
      "h": 78,
      "shape": "rect",
      "color": "#ccfbf1",
      "borderColor": "#0f766e",
      "borderWidth": 3,
      "fontColor": "#0f766e",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "note": "Follett's integration: not domination, not compromise, but a process that produces something neither party brought in. That is exactly He — active merging — and it is what an NDC is for. Belonging is not a state you install; it is the residue of conversations that keep happening.",
      "type": "lg_cond",
      "icon": "rcn_conversation",
      "ovr": {
        "icon": "rcn_conversation"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "crowd",
      "label": "FEAR ⇒ CROWD",
      "x": 1620,
      "y": 1620,
      "w": 84,
      "h": 84,
      "shape": "rect",
      "color": "#fef2f2",
      "borderColor": "#b91c1c",
      "borderWidth": 3,
      "fontColor": "#b91c1c",
      "fontSize": 10,
      "note": "Fear -> Crowd is positive, and Crowd -> Group is negative: a crowd is not a large group, it is the destruction of one. In your frame the crowd also feeds the large-system level NEGATIVELY, where the group feeds it positively. This is the failure mode I called capture by the loudest, and the frame says it is manufactured by fear rather than by numbers alone.",
      "type": "lg_failgrp",
      "icon": "rcn_conflict",
      "ovr": {
        "icon": "rcn_conflict"
      }
